        {
            "id": "service/qnmegF00",
            "name": "CESSDA Vocabulary Service",
            "urls": [
                "https://www.cessda.eu/Tools/Vocabulary-Service"
            ],
            "alternativePIDs": null,
            "nodePID": "21.T15999/CESSDA",
            "description": "<p>The Vocabulary Service offers users the ability to discover, browse, and download controlled vocabularies in various languages. Downloads can be done in SKOS, HTML, and PDF formats, in the chosen languages. The Vocabulary service also allows communities and organisations referred to as Agency to host and publish their own vocabularies for users to search and download. The communities have roles such as Editor, which enables them to create, manage, and translate the vocabularies. The editor also includes an access and user management interface and allows versioning with persistent identifiers and citation of the Controlled Vocabularies (CVs). The following link, <a href=\"https://docs.tech.cessda.eu/content-management/cvs-agency.html\">https://docs.tech.cessda.eu/content-management/cvs-agency.html</a>, provides guidance on registering a community as an Agency. Many of the vocabularies have been developed and maintained by the DDI Alliance and its Controlled Vocabularies Working Group. The Data Documentation Initiative (DDI) is a global standard used to describe data generated by surveys and other observational methods in social, behavioural, economic, and health sciences. Non-English versions of the vocabularies have been supplied by CESSDA members and associated organisations in different countries. The vocabularies allow for data descriptions to be harmonised, such as in the CESSDA Data Catalogue (CDC) service. As DDI vocabularies are utilised worldwide, organisations that want to produce and maintain a language not currently included are encouraged to do so. The same applies to the CESSDA Topic Classification vocabulary. Any interested organisation is encouraged to submit their contact information to the DDI Controlled Vocabularies Working Group or via the \"Send feedback\" button on any page in the CESSDA Vocabulary Service. The service is also available through REST API at https://api.tech.cessda.eu/ by selecting the service in the dropbox.</p>",
            "publishingDate": "2026-03-15",
            "type": "Service",
            "resourceOwner": "provider/ZE281w00",
